      "text": "What it is: AI can build an app in minutes. Proving it works is the real skill and the one that gets you hired. Take a real app, test it, fix what breaks, and prove it performs on Mozark's platform, on real devices. Who can enter: College and university students across India and the US. Open to participants aged 18 and over. All skill levels welcome. You do not need to be a coder. Free to enter. How it works: Register on https://www.mozark.ai/back-to-campus Sign up on Mozark with the same email you registered with - https://id.mozark.ai/signup Explore the Starter Org , a pre-loaded demo space for TCM, Infra and MCP. Create your own organization, named StudentName_Collegename. Invite support@mozark.ai as an admin so we can track your progress. You're all set to start the challenge! What counts as a valid bug: Your bug has to be real to score. Scores: it breaks a key user journey and fails consistently (at least 2 of 3 runs). Doesn't score: typos and minor colour or style tweaks. Scoring: A fixed 100-point scale across the two rounds, plus a separate 50-point bonus. Every point is earned on evidence, not activity. Defined criteria, not a judgment call, so you always know where you stand on the leaderboard. Build it. Test it. Fix it. Make it perform. Register now.",
